\description{
Fits the Acharya-Hainmueller-Xu structural conjoint estimator via a
cross-fitted deep neural network with double/debiased machine
learning (DML) inference.  The DNN flexibly maps respondent
moderators \code{Z} into per-respondent preference weights \code{beta(Z)},
and the DML correction debiases \code{E[beta(Z)]} for the non-parametric
first stage.  Standard errors are clustered at the respondent level.
}
\details{
The returned \code{sc_fit} list contains at least the following fields:
\itemize{
\item \code{theta} -- named p-vector of DML point estimates;
\item \code{vcov} -- full \verb{p x p} clustered variance-covariance;
\item \code{vcov_iid} -- full \verb{p x p} iid variance-covariance (diagnostic);
\item \code{se_ratio_dml_iid} -- list with \code{per_param} and \code{mean};
\item \code{beta_hat} -- N x p matrix of held-out beta(Z);
\item \code{Z} -- N x p_Z matrix of moderators;
\item \code{fold_id} -- integer vector of fold assignments;
\item \code{lambda_obj} -- Lambda(Z) estimation output;
\item \code{call}, \code{formula}, \code{attr_names}, \code{z_names}, \code{respondent_id};
\item \code{K}, \code{hidden}, \code{seed}, \code{n_epochs}, \code{learning_rate}, \code{device},
\code{parallel}, \code{n_cores};
\item \code{loss_traces} -- list of per-fold training loss curves;
\item \code{interaction} -- \code{NULL} unless \code{interactions != "none"}; a list with
the identified feature set (\code{pairs}, \code{feature_names}), the DML
interaction coefficients and clustered variance (\code{theta}, \code{vcov},
\code{se}; the full expanded \code{theta_full} / \code{vcov_full}), the
population-level plugin coefficients (\code{w_hat}; per-fold \code{w_fold}),
the averaged \verb{W_avg = mean(V V')} under \code{"lowrank"} (only the
cross-attribute blocks of \code{W} are identified -- \code{V} itself never
is), the realized-task features \code{F_int} and cross-fitted offsets
(\code{g_offset}, \code{g_offset_ens}, \code{g_offset_task}), and the interaction
block of the orthogonal-score correction (\code{correction_int}).
}
